index 4479b53..1b3b968 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,34 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Browser agent tools
+
+The shared layout exposes client-side WebMCP tools through the React
+`use-webmcp-tool` integration. Registration is feature-detected and cleaned up
+when the layout unmounts during Astro navigation. Use a secure context and a
+browser with WebMCP enabled; browsers without it retain the normal controls.
+
+| Tool | Input | Result |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `open_search` | None | Opens the search flyout and exposes its form |
+| `open_reading_list` | None | Opens the reading-list flyout and exposes its form |
+| `search_articles` | `query` | Articles matching headline or summary, with slugs and URLs |
+| `get_article` | `slug` | Article metadata and body text without navigation or executing article scripts |
+| `get_reading_list` | None | Saved article metadata and URLs for the current session |
+| `update_reading_list` | `slug`, `action`: `add` or `remove` | Updated saved slugs; repeated requests preserve the requested membership |
+
+The open flyouts also expose declarative forms: `search_articles_form` (`query`)
+and `manage_reading_list_form` (`slug`, `action`). Both support automatic submission
+and return JSON results through the agent submit event's `respondWith`. Form
+values are read from `FormData` so agent-filled controls and manual submissions
+use the same handlers. Article loading can briefly disable submission; agents
+can retry after loading or use the site-wide utilities directly.
+
+Requests respect agent cancellation, use the configured Astro base path, and
+return descriptive error results on failure. Bookmark changes update open lists
+and article bookmark buttons. The existing session API remains the source of truth.
+
+Run `pnpm test` for search, bookmark retry/concurrency, cancellation, and HTTP
+failure checks (Node 24+), and `pnpm run build` for the production build. These
+checks do not start an application server.
